{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch77oZFHkuBQvqTnGFkaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"contract_version\":\"agent3-grounding-judgment-v5\",\"verdicts\":[{\"statement_id\":\"claim:c7\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The current triage guidance (v1.3, effective 2026-09-26) contains this sentence, and the quote matches it exactly.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"claim:c9\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"None of the cited messages states a cause. The reports describe symptoms only, and the QA tutor notes only that the downloaded WAV plays normally.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"summary:s1\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"Three tutors (U9106, U9107, U9108) report stalls on AUD-741, AUD-754 and AUD-768. QA tutor U9104 reproduced the stuck clock on AUD-754.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"summary:s2\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The guidance says to collect task IDs, browser versions and reproduction steps and to send one scoped engineering incident. No cause is stated in the cited messages.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"detail:d1\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"U9106 reports the sound stopping after dragging the waveform back to the start, with the clock at 0:00, on AUD-741. The follow-up message gives Firefox 132.0.2 and says reopening restores playback until the next seek.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"detail:d2\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"U9107 reports the clock never advancing after the scrubber moves on AUD-754 in Chrome 131.0.6778.85. QA tutor U9104 reproduced the stuck clock and says the downloaded WAV plays normally.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"detail:d3\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"U9108's message matches: endless spinner after jump-back on AUD-768 in Firefox 132.0.2, after playback had already worked.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"detail:d4\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"QA tutor U9104 asked for the task ID and browser build and said a second reproduction was needed before filing. U9106, the thread starter, supplied both.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"detail:d5\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"Team lead U9101 asked the thread starter U9108 to keep the affected task open and add browser and task details to one report.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"action\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"Premise claim:c7 is supported. The rejected premises c1-c4 are not essential, because the action's content rests on the cited member messages and the guidance. The instruction matches the guidance. The draft names no concrete route, states that the cause is unconfirmed, and notes that reproduction steps are still to be added. The 'check seek handling' request is a modest suggestion consistent with the reports.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"action:rationale\",\"verdict\":\"PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The guidance applies to a reproducible freeze after seeking, and AUD-754 was reproduced. AUD-741 and AUD-768 are single-tutor reports, and reproduction steps are not yet collected. 'Reports match a reproducible freeze' overstates this for all three.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"action:need\",\"verdict\":\"PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"Three tutors in separate threads report stalls and one was reproduced by a QA tutor. 'No engineering report is shown' is an absence claim that the evidence is consistent with but does not establish. The team lead did ask for one report in the AUD-768 thread.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"review_note\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The threads contain no reproduction steps for AUD-754 or AUD-768. The AUD-741 and AUD-768 threads have no second reproduction.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"resolution:member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The thread ends with U9106 supplying details and shows no cause or fix.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"resolution:member_77774044871dcbe2f1dfe164\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The thread ends with the QA tutor confirming reproduction and shows no cause or fix.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"resolution:member_c945ef64798eef3548b64165\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"The team lead asked for details in one report, and the thread shows no answer or fix.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"severity:rationale\",\"verdict\":\"PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"Three tutors on three tasks report stalls after seeking and one was reproduced. 'The same kind of stall' is slightly generalised, since AUD-768 reports a spinner after jump-back.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"severity:signal:HIGH[3]\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"Three distinct tutors report comparable problems on three tasks, within about an hour (08:05 to 09:04) on the same day.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"reporter:U9106\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"U9106's own message reports the sound stopping on AUD-741.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"reporter:U9107\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"U9107's own message reports the clock not advancing on AUD-754.\"},{\"statement_id\":\"reporter:U9108\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"rationale\":\"U9108's own message reports the endless spinner on AUD-768.\"}],\"action_sufficiency\":{\"verdict\":\"SUFFICIENT\",\"essential_statement_ids\":[\"claim:c7\"],\"rationale\":\"The supported guidance premise justifies sending one scoped engineering incident with browser versions. The draft carries the reported facts, flags the unconfirmed cause and the missing reproduction steps, and names no concrete route.\"},\"source_consistency\":{\"assessed_evidence_ids\":[\"k:pilot-audio-incident-triage@1.3:3b2b70f0\",\"k:pilot-media-input-quality-faq@1.1:00309a9c\"],\"relations\":[],\"declared_conflict_checks\":[]}}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12963,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2105,"output_tokens_details":{"thinkin